From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin <robinei@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:46:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] crocus: don't snoop upload staging textures on non-LLC parts

crocus makes every PIPE_USAGE_STAGING BO snooped (I915_CACHING_CACHED)
on parts without LLC, which also makes it non-reusable. That suits
staging textures the CPU reads back, but not upload staging textures:
the CPU writes them once and the GPU blits from them, so snooping only
makes the GPU's reads slower and costs a fresh BO with a clflush for
every upload. The common desktop-GL upload glTexSubImage2D(GL_BGRA)
into a GL_RGBA8 texture (SDL's opengl renderer, Wine) takes this path
for every frame.

On a GPD Win 1 (Cherry Trail, MIPI DSI panel) these snooped reads also
stall the display pipe: the DSI controller's DPI FIFO underruns about
0.5 ms after the blit starts and the picture flashes or splits. With an
SDL-style test (853x480 XRGB8888 streaming texture uploaded every frame,
10 min each): 205 underruns and a 3.73 ms mean upload (>5 ms in 20 % of
frames) with snooped staging, 0 underruns and 1.14 ms (never >5 ms)
without.

Keep snooping for staging textures with any binding other than
PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW (the state tracker's readback paths use render
target or image bindings) and for read maps in crocus_map_copy_region;
mark write-only copy-region staging as sampler view.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/crocus/crocus_resource.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/crocus/crocus_resource.c b/src/gallium/drivers/crocus/crocus_resource.c
index e054fca..eba6d4d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/crocus/crocus_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/crocus/crocus_resource.c
@@ -662,7 +662,16 @@ crocus_resource_create_with_modifiers(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
    const char *name = "miptree";
 
    unsigned int flags = 0;
-   if (templ->usage == PIPE_USAGE_STAGING)
+   /* Staging textures the CPU reads back (render target or image binding,
+    * or a read map in crocus_map_copy_region) are snooped so that CPU reads
+    * are cached. Upload staging textures (sampler view only: the CPU writes
+    * them once, the GPU blits from them) are not: on non-LLC parts the GPU's
+    * snooped reads of them are slow, the BO cannot be reused (a fresh one
+    * with a clflush every upload), and on a GPD Win 1 (CHV) these reads make
+    * the MIPI DSI display pipe stall (DPI FIFO underruns, flashing picture).
+    */
+   if (templ->usage == PIPE_USAGE_STAGING &&
+       templ->bind != PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW)
       flags |= BO_ALLOC_COHERENT;
 
    /* Scanout buffers need to be WC. */
@@ -1165,6 +1174,10 @@ crocus_map_copy_region(struct crocus_transfer *map)
 
    struct pipe_resource templ = (struct pipe_resource) {
       .usage = PIPE_USAGE_STAGING,
+      /* write-only: an upload source for the blit, not snooped (see
+       * crocus_resource_create_with_modifiers)
+       */
+      .bind = (xfer->usage & PIPE_MAP_READ) ? 0 : PIPE_BIND_SAMPLER_VIEW,
       .width0 = box->width + extra,
       .height0 = box->height,
       .depth0 = 1,
